// Adversarial stress: Burnout protocol with Perfect-bump driver — Scatter layout.
//
// The heat contract is most meaningfully stressed when mega_bump_charged is
// repeatedly consumed. AlwaysPerfect input guarantees every bump is a Perfect
// grade, which in turn guarantees BumpPerformed fires with a grade the system
// can act on. Combined with the Scatter layout (irregular cell spacing drives
// non-trivial bolt trajectories and breaker movement), the breaker accumulates
// heat quickly on moving ticks, arms mega_bump_charged at heat = 1.0, and fires
// burnout_on_bump on the next BumpPerformed — resetting heat to 0.0 and
// dispatching a shockwave and DamageBoost. This scenario targets three failure
// paths not strongly exercised by burnout_chaos (which relies on probabilistic
// bumps):
//
//   1. heat = 1.0 → bump → reset race per tick: with AlwaysPerfect the bolt
//      reaches the breaker on every descent. If the breaker has been moving,
//      heat reaches 1.0 before the bump and burnout_on_bump resets it. The
//      sequencing contract — burnout_update_heat runs before burnout_on_bump —
//      must hold every tick. If the ordering edge is lost, burnout_on_bump sees
//      the OLD heat value (from the prior tick's update), does not see
//      mega_bump_charged, and the reset is missed. On the next tick,
//      burnout_update_heat finds heat >= 1.0 - EPSILON and re-arms the charge,
//      but heat at 1.0 + dt/fill_duration would exceed 1.0 before the
//      `.min(1.0)` clamp fires. BurnoutHeatClamped catches any momentary
//      overshoot.
//
//   2. BurnoutDamageBoost single-shot pierce guard under repeated Perfect bumps:
//      burnout_amplify_damage is single-shot — it removes BurnoutDamageBoost
//      via deferred commands after the first BoltImpactCell. With AlwaysPerfect
//      driving rapid bumps, a new BurnoutDamageBoost is installed every time
//      mega_bump_charged is consumed. If the deferred removal from tick N-1
//      does not flush before burnout_on_bump in tick N installs a new one, the
//      bolt carries two overlapping DamageBoost components (or the ECS archetype
//      collapses to the newer one silently). NoNaN catches NaN from a corrupted
//      multiplier; NoEntityLeaks catches any double-installed component whose
//      remove command misfired.
//
//   3. still_threshold + mega_bump_charged co-fire: if the breaker is stationary
//      and heat reaches the still_threshold (1.5 s still), the instant-drain
//      fires and sets heat = 0.0 and mega_bump_charged = false. On a frame where
//      the breaker was ALSO stationary last tick AND AlwaysPerfect fires a
//      BumpPerformed in the same FixedUpdate, burnout_on_bump checks
//      mega_bump_charged (which was just set to false by the still-threshold
//      branch) and skips the boost install. BurnoutHeatClamped validates that
//      the co-fire path leaves heat exactly at 0.0 and still_timer at 0.0, not
//      at any transient value.
//
// 3000 frames with allow_early_end: false sustains the mega-bump cycle across
// node restarts. 16 runs with varied Scatter seeds explore diverse bolt
// trajectories and bump-rate distributions.
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Scatter",
    input: Perfect(AlwaysPerfect),
    max_frames: 3000,
    disallowed_failures: [
        NoNaN,
        BoltInBounds,
        BreakerInBounds,
        BoltSpeedAccurate,
        ValidDashState,
        BreakerCountReasonable,
        NoEntityLeaks,
        BoltCountReasonable,
        BurnoutHeatClamped,
    ],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    stress: (runs: 16, parallelism: 16),
    seed: 8813,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 10, mutation: InjectProtocol(kind_name: "Burnout")),
    ],
)
